Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:16:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] drm/asahi: g15: renumber the TA/FS stamps before the TA
 stamp wraps
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The TA stamp of render ordinal n is stamp_seed(TA_SEED, n): it steps by
0x100 and wraps after 0x860000 renders, about six hours of desktop. With
the stamp_seed() from before commit 7ccdfe85843d ("drm/asahi: wrap G15
stamps through zero"), which skipped zero and went from 0xffffff00 back
to 0x100 there, the firmware stopped at render 8781824 with "DAG: Non
Sequential Stamp Updates seen ... stampValue 0x100" and the GPU was lost
until reboot. Since that commit the stamps wrap through zero; whether
the firmware takes that wrap has not been tried.

Add an offset to the render ordinal used for the TA/FS stamps and, when
g15_stamp_reseed_margin is set, renumber both stamps from their seeds at
the first publication with nothing in flight inside that margin: write
the seeds to the user and firmware stamps, reset the engine targets and
move the offset so the next render counts as ordinal 1, as after boot.
The offset is taken modulo the 2^24 ordinals after which stamp_seed()
repeats (STAMP_PERIOD). The stamps then never reach the wrap.
g15_stamp_base starts the count near the wrap, to test this in seconds
instead of hours.

Both parameters default to 0, which keeps the stamps exactly as before.

Tested on a J516C, together with the next commit, on integration/aurora
with the earlier stamp_seed() and the offset taken modulo its period of
0xffffff ordinals: from g15_stamp_base 2000 renders before the wrap with
a margin of 1000, the stamps were renumbered at render 1000 and 3003
renders retired; in desktop use, one boot renumbered at renders 8681824
and 17363648. On this base, modulo 0xffffff would give the render after
the first renumbering ordinal 0, whose targets the seeds already meet,
and the one after the second ordinal -1, a TA target below the seed.

